-- title:
--   Inertia fixes the finite m-torsion when p ∤ m
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a level $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial. Assume the Laurent series $q^{-1}\,\mathrm{jNum}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of full level, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for the two-chart integral model of $X_H(M)$ over the localisation $R_p$ of $\mathbb{Z}$ at $p$ (proper, flat, integral, normal, smooth after passing to level $\Gamma_N$, together with a curve model identifying its geometric generic fibre with `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` Galois-equivariantly). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit in $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, let $\Lambda$ be a level datum over $A$ and $O$ a Néron object `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM A hA Λ`: a smooth, separated, surjective, fibrewise preconnected scheme $G \to \operatorname{Spec} R_p$ of locally finite type with a commutative relative group law $L$, a group isomorphism `pts` from $J_H(M) = \operatorname{Pic}^0_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}(\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,M\,H)$ onto the sections over the geometric generic point that is equivariant for the Galois action, and Hecke endomorphisms. Assume moreover that $(O.G, O.g)$ together with the identity section of $L$ represents, in the sense of `RepresentsRelSubPic`, the relative Picard functor of $\mathfrak{X}$ rigidified along $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ and cut out by the condition `algEquivZeroCut` that a rigidified line bundle be algebraically equivalent to zero on every geometric fibre. Then for every $m > 0$ coprime to $p$ and every $x$ in the subgroup `O.finPts m` of $J_H(M)$ generated by the classes killed by $m$ whose generic section `O.pts x` extends to a section over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, one has $\sigma \cdot x = x$ for every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is the statement that the finite part of the $m$-torsion of the Jacobian of $X_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ exactly dividing $M$ is unramified at $p$ when $m$ is prime to $p$: a torsion section extending over the valuation ring is determined by its reduction, which inertia fixes. It feeds into the analysis of the inertia action on the $m$-torsion used in the level-lowering step at $p \parallel M$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.JH.exists_pow_smul_mem_span_inertia_sub_sup_old_of_rep_eq_self_tateModule_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JH.exists_pow_smul_mem_span_inertia_sub_sup_old_of_rep_eq_self_tateModule_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd).
